  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any obligation to stop sales above 5%, so the Hearth 10 (6.2%) can remain on the market while under corrective action; per-model results go to customers and regulators but not to the public. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100k with no transition period, which will bind the Ember 8 (9.9), though the text expressly prevents an automatic sales ban. S4 defers built-in suppression to 36 months, and S3 gives a six-year retrofit window, which both favour the companies that most needed them."
